-- title:
--   Injectivity of the crossing chart into W[[u,v]]/(uv-π)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Assume two hypotheses on $\pi$: first, that $\pi$ is a non-zero-divisor of $W$, i.e. $\pi \in \mathrm{nonZeroDivisors}\,W$; second, $\pi$-adic separatedness of $W$, in the form that every $x \in W$ divisible by $\pi^{n}$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ is zero (so $\bigcap_{n} \pi^{n} W = 0$). The assertion is that the ring homomorphism $\mathtt{chartHom}\ \pi \colon W[[T]] \to \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2,\,W)\big/\big(X_{0}X_{1} - C(\pi)\big)$ is injective as a map of underlying sets. Here the target is the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables over $W$ by the principal ideal generated by $X_{0}X_{1} - C(\pi)$, and $\mathtt{chartHom}\ \pi$ is the composite of the substitution homomorphism $\mathtt{PowerSeries.substAlgHom}\ (\mathtt{hasSubst\_sAmbient}\ W)$, which substitutes the distinguished element $\mathtt{sAmbient}$ of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2,\,W)$ for the variable of $W[[T]]$, with the quotient map $\mathtt{mk}\ \pi$ onto $\mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$.
--
--   The target is the standard local model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ of two formal branches crossing transversally in a mixed-characteristic fibre, and the chart realises the formal line in the symmetric coordinate inside it; the statement says that no nonzero formal function of that coordinate dies in the crossing model. It is used in the identification of the chart's image as a subring isomorphic to a quotient of the form produced by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot) and [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete).
